Subject: PostgreSQL 18.6 on Fil-C staging with a zmark_shared main segment
Origin: Filnix (prototype evidence for docs/zmark-shared.md, not used by a Nix build)

Applies to pristine PostgreSQL 18.6. Build with filcc-staging from the
zmark-shared branch, CFLAGS="-O2 -g -Wno-int-conversion", and run with
huge_pages=off. See docs/zmark-shared.md, section PostgreSQL.

zmark_shared changes:
- sysv_shmem.c: zmark_shared(ptr) after the main segment's mmap.
- shm_mq.c: sender and receiver as ProcNumber + 1, not PGPROC *.
- parallel.c: the leader as parallel_leader_proc_number, and the
  SERIALIZABLEXACT as an offset from ProcGlobal, not pointers, in the DSM.
- aio.c, aio_init.c, aio_internal.h: the issuer's resowner, resowner_node
  and report_return in a backend-private array indexed by handle id.
- aio_io.c: iovecs of IOs on local buffers in backend-private memory.

Single-process Fil-C porting, shared with the release-toolchain port
(T-01a1ac20): no x86 asm in atomics.h, s_lock.h and pg_bitutils.h; Datum as
char * (postgres.h, nodes.h, network.c, numeric.c, varlena.c); xlogprefetcher's
private pointer as void *; sort_template.h's ST_SWAPN through memcpy;
ExpandedObjectHeader padding so its TOAST pointers are 8-byte aligned; and
libpq's exit check allowing filc_allocate_without_exiting.

